{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "notes": [
    "Native UI action-to-state observation is not display presentation or decoder seek latency.",
    "Default menu measurements use an idle player, a fixed locale, screen geometry/DPI and the same native automation method.",
    "Each adapter must verify owned process identity, a false precondition, native action, and a true postcondition; absent adapters/permissions are unranked.",
    "Requested actions requiring frame presentation stay pending until a content-aware presentation collector exists.",
    "Applications use their default window sizes; actual bounds are retained as evidence. This is not an equal-viewport comparison.",
    "Every action has total, dispatch and observation latency, CPU time, post-action RSS and RSS growth events. Missing evidence remains unranked.",
    "Linux uses native pointer input at observed owned accessibility bounds for every entrant. Hidden zero-area menu nodes and existing toolbar controls are not popup evidence."
  ],
